Build upstream LoopAlgorithm in Swift 5 language mode on Linux.

PrecomputedInsulinInput (#29) parallelizes with DispatchQueue.concurrentPerform,
relying on Darwin declaring its closure non-@Sendable. swift-corelibs-libdispatch
declares it @Sendable, so Swift 6 strict concurrency rejects the build on Linux
(Swift 6.0 and 6.1.2). Each iteration writes a distinct index, so the code is
safe; Swift 5 mode only relaxes the compile-time check. Upstream tests: 140/140
pass on Linux with this patch.

diff --git a/Package.swift b/Package.swift
index 92287f9..d0e4a2d 100644
--- a/Package.swift
+++ b/Package.swift
@@ -36,5 +36,5 @@ let package = Package(
             ]
         )
     ],
-    swiftLanguageModes: [.v6]
+    swiftLanguageModes: [.v5]
 )
